CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts _ --unwind 2 --unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[g\.loop_assigns\.\d+\] line \d+ Check assigns clause inclusion for loop g\.0: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[.*unwind.*\] .*: FAILURE$
--
The check that the assigns clause of g's loop is included in that of the
loop that calls g loops over the clause's targets: DFCC unwinds it as
far as the largest assigns clause, as its other loops over write sets,
rather than as --unwind says (2 here, for 7 targets).
